  "attempt": "Let G on H0 direct-sum H1 have self-adjoint block form [A,C*;C,D], with D>=delta I for delta>0. If A>=||C||^2/delta times I, then G>=0. More exactly, when D is invertible, G>=0 iff D>=0 and A-C*D^(-1)C>=0. In contrast, on an infinite-dimensional tail, every finite-rank F satisfies ||delta I-F||>=delta. Thus a known positive essential tail must be retained and certified by a Schur complement; treating the entire operator as a small finite-rank norm remainder is impossible below its essential norm.",
